    "finding": "The contextual narrative did not grow. Per printed statement it is unchanged -- 71 words against 70 -- while the demand text more than doubled, 88 against 181. All of the growth is in the text that states what to do, which is what an itemised marking scheme forces onto the paper — a lead-in for each apartado, a sentence for each quantum inside it, and a printed price for both. The dossier had been attributing the reading load to the competency items; on this measurement the competency wrapper is the same size per statement as in 2025 and the granularity is the whole of the increase.",
    "caveat": "One 2026 item (C1, the waves option) states its demands in the apartado lead-in and does not number them, so the lead-in/sub-demand split is not clean item by item. Their SUM — the demand text — is, and it is the quantity the finding rests on."
